{
  "identity": {
    "text": "It was interesting. I went at eleven in the morning and spoke to the manager of the events department.\n\nThe vacancy was for a weekend workshop assistant. I sent the application on Wednesday. The employer wanted someone to help visitors find materials.\n\nYes. I described a garden event where my colleague and I worked as a team. I showed a certificate from a short art course as one qualification. I also brought a copy of my application for the manager.\n\nThey asked how I would help a customer who arrived late. I said I would listen, check the task list and ask an employee if I was unsure.\n\nYes. The hourly wage was fourteen pounds. The manager also mentioned a monthly salary, but that was for a different full-time position.\n\nNo. They will contact each candidate next Tuesday. My goal was to speak clearly, and I felt successful in giving my example.\n\nI will resume my library volunteering on Sunday. I enjoy that service, and I want to build a reliable work routine for my career.\n\nYes. A new assistant starts by preparing tables before visitors arrive. I wrote it in my notes, because this opportunity could teach me a new skill.",
